{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hey, buddy.",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 0.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Hi, dad. I'm Doctor. Asant.",
   "start": 1.22,
   "end": 3.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Can you give me his full name and birthday just so I know I've got the right chart?",
   "start": 4.24,
   "end": 8.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Mateo Villanueva, April 2nd, 2019. I'm his dad, Andres.",
   "start": 9.41,
   "end": 14.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks, Andres. So Mateo, I hear your throat hurts.",
   "start": 14.93,
   "end": 18.31
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Yeah, he's been complaining since Saturday. No, wait, Friday.",
   "start": 19.27,
   "end": 23.05
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It was Friday night after his soccer game.",
   "start": 23.65,
   "end": 25.87
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "He said it hurt to swallow, and then Sunday he got a fever.",
   "start": 26.35,
   "end": 29.57
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How high has the fever gotten?",
   "start": 30.41,
   "end": 32.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "The highest was one hundred two point four last night. I gave him ibuprofen this morning at like seven, so that might be bringing it down.",
   "start": 33.12,
   "end": 41.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good to know.",
   "start": 41.74,
   "end": 42.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Mateo, does your tummy hurt at all? He said his stomach hurt yesterday. Didn't throw up, though. Okay, and he cough? No, not really.",
   "start": 42.82,
   "end": 52.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Runny -nose or stuffy -nose?",
   "start": 52.39,
   "end": 54.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "No, that's kind of why I thought this isn't just a cold. A mom from his class texted that there's strep going around at Brookside Elementary.",
   "start": 55.43,
   "end": 63.59
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Yeah, we've been seeing a lot of it this month. Any rash on his body?",
   "start": 64.55,
   "end": 68.51
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "I didn't see one. Is he drinking okay? Drinking, yes. Eating not so much.",
   "start": 69.15,
   "end": 75.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Popsicles, mostly. Popsicles are perfect, honestly. Now I see in the chart he's allergic to amoxicillin.",
   "start": 75.86,
   "end": 82.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Is that right? Yeah, when he was three he got hives all over,",
   "start": 83.32,
   "end": 87.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "like big red welts from the pink amoxicillin.",
   "start": 87.8,
   "end": 90.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "No trouble breathing or anything, just the hives. Okay, that's helpful. Any other medicines, any daily medicines? No, just the ibuprofen when he needs it.",
   "start": 91.2,
   "end": 101.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "All right. Vitals today he weighs 20 kilograms, that's 44 pounds. temperature is 101 .9, heart rate 112. Mateo, can you open really big and say, ah, great job. Okay, his tonsils are swollen and red and there's white stuff on them and some little red spots on the roof of his mouth. The glands in the front of his neck are swollen and tender. Ears look normal, lungs are clear and I don't see any rash. I'm going to do a quick strep swab, it takes about 10 minutes.",
   "start": 102.63,
   "end": 136.81
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Sure, he's gonna hate it, but okay. It's quick, I promise.",
   "start": 137.63,
   "end": 141.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Mateo count to three with me.",
   "start": 142.21,
   "end": 143.69
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "You did it, buddy. All right, the rapid strep came back positive. So this is strep throat. Okay, so what can he take, since he can't have amoxicillin?",
   "start": 144.11,
   "end": 154.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Since his reaction was hives and not anything severe like swelling or trouble breathing, Cefilxin is a safe choice. The dose is twenty milligrams per kilogram, twice a day. At 20 kilograms, that's 400 milligrams twice a day. The liquid is 250 milligrams per 5 milliliters, so 8 milliliters twice a day for 10 days.",
   "start": 154.61,
   "end": 177.21
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "8 milliliters, twice a day, 10 days, got it.",
   "start": 177.95,
   "end": 180.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "For the throat pain and fever, ibuprofen is fine. His dose is 200 milligrams, so 10 milliliters of the children's liquid every 6 to 8 hours as needed, with some food.",
   "start": 181.63,
   "end": 193.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "When can he go back to school? He's already missed Monday.",
   "start": 193.99,
   "end": 197.81
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Once he's had at least twelve hours of the antibiotic and he's fever -free, he can go back. So probably Thursday. I can put a school note in the portal.",
   "start": 198.75,
   "end": 207.87
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Great. The portal e -mail is AndresDartVillanueva at example .com. And um, my wife woke up with a scratchy throat today. Should she get the medicine too?",
   "start": 208.85,
   "end": 219.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "She'd need to be checked by her own doctor. We don't treat without testing. Same goes for anyone else in the house who gets sick.",
   "start": 219.19,
   "end": 227.65
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "Okay, makes sense.",
   "start": 228.67,
   "end": 229.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Swap out his toothbrush after a day or two on the medicine. And if he starts drooling, can't swallow his own spit, can't open his mouth all the way or has trouble breathing, go straight to the emergency room. If he's not better in two or three days, call us. Okay,",
   "start": 230.17,
   "end": 247.59
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "caregiver",
   "text": "and the number you have on file, 555 -0118. That's my cell, so call that one. Perfect, I'll send it now. And how'd the soccer game go, by the way? They last four to one, but he scored the one.",
   "start": 247.93,
   "end": 262.31
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Nice, feel better, Mateo.",
   "start": 262.99,
   "end": 264.63
  }
 ],
